From 7a93efd8de4d8a264489f02bb1040de469fdbde1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ole Algoritme <olealgoritme@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 14:59:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nak: a PLOP3 of a comparison and a predicate becomes the
 comparison's accumulator (NAK_PLOP_FOLD)

FSETP and ISETP compute (a cmp b) AND/OR/XOR p in one instruction, but
NAK emitted the comparison and a separate PLOP3 for an iand/ior of a
comparison with another predicate: 413 PLOP3s in the six heaviest Steel
Nomad fragment shaders, where the reference compiler's code has 6.

opt_fold_plop3_setp moves a single-use plain comparison down to the
PLOP3 that combines it with one other predicate (its sources are SSA
values, so they still hold there) and makes that predicate the
accumulator; a negated comparison result flips the comparison
(ordered <-> unordered for floats).  The accumulator must be in the
comparison's register file.

Offline, GB202: Steel Nomad fragment 143389 -> 142733 instructions,
CS2 fragment -0.35%.
